Dr. Khalifa: Pardon.

01:03:16.000 --> 01:03:19.000
Dr. Sabahi: So, it doesn't have anything to do with SHAFA'AT (Intercession)?

01:03:19.000 --> 01:03:22.000
Dr. Khalifa: No. It actually proves there is no SHAFA'AT (Intercession).

01:03:25.000 --> 01:03:33.000
Because it's only the believers who will, who will be helped, and the believers are going to Heaven anyway.

01:03:34.000 --> 01:03:40.000
The disbelievers and the hypocrites cannot be helped, so what's the use of SHAFA'AT? So, this is what the, the Quranic position is.

01:03:40.000 --> 01:03:45.000
In fact, the Quranic position is that every one of us,

01:03:45.000 --> 01:03:50.000
IN SHAA ALLAH, when we go to Heaven, we'll say "please God, I want my mother with me. I love her very much."

01:03:50.000 --> 01:03:51.000
Ok?

01:03:51.000 --> 01:03:53.000
And this is SHAFA'AT.

01:03:53.000 --> 01:03:58.000
You will say it. I will say it. Everybody will say it, IN SHAA ALLAH, in Heaven.

01:03:58.000 --> 01:04:05.000
And now, this SHAFA'AT is useful if the mother is a good person that is already going to Heaven.

01:04:06.000 --> 01:04:11.000
If the mother was not to go to Heaven, this SHAFA'AT will not do any good. Therefore, it is really useless, but

01:04:11.000 --> 01:04:13.000
we will say it anyway, out of emotion.

01:04:15.000 --> 01:04:19.000
So, this is the understanding of SHAFA'AT. And this is exactly what this verse was saying.

01:04:20.000 --> 01:04:24.000
It is saying when the messenger asks, prays for forgiveness,

01:04:24.000 --> 01:04:28.000
Dr. Khalifa: for it will be accepted for the believers, but not for the hypocrites or the disbelievers.

01:04:29.000 --> 01:04:31.000
A man: (unintelligible)

