Dr. Khalifa: And in Arabic, too. And English. And Egyptian.

01:08:05.000 --> 01:08:08.000
Dr. Khalifa: Did we finish Sura 63? Ok. Go ahead and finish it.

01:08:08.000 --> 01:08:09.000
Catherine: Verse 9.

01:08:09.000 --> 01:08:17.000
[63:9] O you who believe, do not be distracted by your business and your children from the commemoration of GOD. Those who do this are losers.

01:08:17.000 --> 01:08:27.000
[63:10] And spend in charity from what we provided for you before death comes to the one of you, and then say, "My Lord, if You postpone this for a short while, I will be charitable and righteous!"

01:08:27.000 --> 01:08:36.000
[63:11] GOD never postpones the end for any soul once the predetermined time has come. GOD is Cognizant of everything you do.

01:08:37.000 --> 01:08:42.000
The easiest thing in the world to do is to be distracted by those that we care about the most.

01:08:42.000 --> 01:08:48.000
And God warns us against that. In other verses, He says that these may be enemies of ours, we do need to be cautious of that

01:08:48.000 --> 01:08:50.000
and avoid idolatry.

01:08:51.000 --> 01:08:57.000
Spending in charity is so easy if we know that nothing we have came from us or will go with us anywhere.

01:08:57.000 --> 01:09:03.000
It comes from God. It's not ours to start with. And if we give it in charity, we give it only where it was meant to go.

01:09:04.000 --> 01:09:06.000
Verse 11 says,

01:09:06.000 --> 01:09:08.000
[63:11] GOD never postpones the end for any soul ...

01:09:08.000 --> 01:09:13.000
And once the time comes, it's come and there's nothing more that you can do after the Day of Resurrection.

01:09:13.000 --> 01:09:20.000
But there is so much mercy from God, and we have so many chances before that Day. So many. They're limitless.

01:09:20.000 --> 01:09:26.000
As long as we live, we have a, we have a chance, an opportunity. God constantly provides those opportunities

01:09:26.000 --> 01:09:31.000
for the hypocrites to repent, for us to continue to work right up until the last moment.

01:09:31.000 --> 01:09:35.000
That verse 11 sounds very final,

01:09:35.000 --> 01:09:41.000
but when we know the mercy of God and what He provides for us on a minute-to-minute, second-to-second basis in this world,

01:09:41.000 --> 01:09:44.000
it's, it's extraordinary.

01:09:44.000 --> 01:09:48.000
And, and it doesn't need to frighten us. We just, we just need to know that, that there is a limit.

01:09:49.000 --> 01:09:52.000
And once we've reached it, it's over. We have no more to do.

01:09:54.000 --> 01:09:56.000
Catherine: Any other comments or questions?

01:09:59.000 --> 01:10:01.000
Farhad: May I ask a question?

01:10:01.000 --> 01:10:02.000
Dr. Khalifa: Yeah. Go ahead.

01:10:02.000 --> 01:10:07.000
Dr. Khalifa: Well, let's get to the, and just thank Catherine for an excellent Quranic study.

01:10:07.000 --> 01:10:10.000
Catherine: I can go to 114 in 10 minutes. You said you want me to (unintelligible)

01:10:12.000 --> 01:10:14.000
Dr. Khalifa: Now, we'll get to general questions.

01:10:15.000 --> 01:10:16.000
Dr. Khalifa: Farhad.

01:10:16.000 --> 01:10:21.000
Farhad: (unintelligible), then we are locked. There are

01:10:21.000 --> 01:10:25.000
many, many (unintelligible) and why.

01:10:28.000 --> 01:10:34.000
Sometimes a group of people think as (unintelligible), toward a Sura and Aya (verse).

01:10:34.000 --> 01:10:37.000
(unintelligible)

01:10:38.000 --> 01:10:46.000
What is the criterion to, to order of what this was more important than this?

01:10:46.000 --> 01:10:48.000
(unintelligible).

01:10:48.000 --> 01:10:53.000
Is there any criteria like that? Or that's my suggestion.

01:10:54.000 --> 01:10:55.000
Farhad: (unintelligible)

01:10:55.000 --> 01:10:57.000
Dr. Khalifa: Everything God said, excuse me...

01:10:57.000 --> 01:11:05.000
Farhad: No, excuse me. The number of times that a subject involves being mentioned, is that (unintelligible)? so I heard.

01:11:05.000 --> 01:11:06.000
Dr. Khalifa: That's a good sign, yeah.

01:11:06.000 --> 01:11:07.000
Farhad: Good sign.

01:11:07.000 --> 01:11:10.000
Dr. Khalifa: But all, all of them are important. All the laws are important.

01:11:11.000 --> 01:11:19.000
I wanna go back to the Friday business. Remember that the title of the Sura is named after the Prayer, "Friday."

01:11:19.000 --> 01:11:22.000
It is a Sura in the Quran entitled "Friday."

01:11:22.000 --> 01:11:24.000
And the commandment is there saying

01:11:25.000 --> 01:11:28.000
[62:9] O you who believe, when the Salat Prayer is announced on Friday, ...

01:11:28.000 --> 01:11:28.000
go

01:11:28.000 --> 01:11:30.000
[62:9] ... and drop all business. ...

01:11:30.000 --> 01:11:31.000
That's the commandment.

01:11:31.000 --> 01:11:33.000
Dr. Khalifa: All the commandments of God are important.

01:11:36.000 --> 01:11:40.000
Farhad: Why is "La Elaha Ella Allah" more important than anything else?

01:11:40.000 --> 01:11:41.000
Dr. Khalifa: Cause this is the basic requirement,

01:11:41.000 --> 01:11:42.000
Farhad: Yeah, that's right.

01:11:42.000 --> 01:11:45.000
Dr. Khalifa: you know. I mean, if it's not there, nothing else exists.

01:11:46.000 --> 01:11:54.000
Everything else will be in vain. I mean, a person can be truthful and honest and

01:11:54.000 --> 01:11:58.000
is a very nice person, but he does not believe in God, and all his work is in vain.

01:12:00.000 --> 01:12:10.000
So, "La Elaha Ella Allah" goes without saying. Then, after that, all the commandments are very important,

01:12:10.000 --> 01:12:12.000
Dr. Khalifa: every single one of them.

01:12:13.000 --> 01:12:17.000
Farhad: For example, can you say Salat is more important than Zakat?

01:12:18.000 --> 01:12:19.000
Dr. Khalifa: No.

01:12:19.000 --> 01:12:21.000
Farhad: Because it's mentioned more than...

01:12:22.000 --> 01:12:27.000
Dr. Khalifa: Actually, they are both usually mentioned together, Salat and Zakat.

01:12:27.000 --> 01:12:28.000
Farhad: Or Fasting.

01:12:29.000 --> 01:12:31.000
Dr. Khalifa: Fasting is very important.

01:12:31.000 --> 01:12:37.000
You're disobeying God if you don't fast. You're disobeying God if you don't do the Zakat. You're disobeying God if you don't do the Prayer.

01:12:37.000 --> 01:12:40.000
You're disobeying God if you lie or cheat.

01:12:40.000 --> 01:12:44.000
Dr. Khalifa: So, take your pick. It's very expensive if you...

01:12:44.000 --> 01:12:51.000
A woman: But that, that also, I think it's important to say that God knows what's true and we have to do God all gifts,

01:12:51.000 --> 01:12:54.000
A woman: you know, when people who can't do it, gives us alternatives.

01:12:54.000 --> 01:13:01.000
Dr. Khalifa: Well, it's our choice, you know. You can put your finger in the fire or not. You can... It's up to you.

01:13:01.000 --> 01:13:05.000
I mean, it's God, God left us, left it, left it up to us.

01:13:10.000 --> 01:13:12.000
You heard Jahan today.

01:13:13.000 --> 01:13:18.000
If he didn't wanna do the push-ups, he will, he will think that God is doing everything, not him.

01:13:20.000 --> 01:13:23.000
So, it's as simple as that.

01:13:23.000 --> 01:13:26.000
We're celebrating Laila's birthday today.

01:13:29.000 --> 01:13:31.000
I don't mean to embarrass you.

01:13:33.000 --> 01:13:37.000
